From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 06:16:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] presentation: panorama layout skips per-item work while
 content is unchanged
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A fling remeasured every placed cell even when the items, spans, and
lane widths had not changed. On a 2000-item shelf that per-item walk
showed up as stutter once the finger was released.

The layout cache now keys on a content epoch. While the epoch, count,
and lane widths match, it reuses the previous placement instead of
running the per-item work again. A band change bumps the epoch and
reflows.

与 mihon-harmony 0025 同源. The three shared panorama files are copied
byte for byte from that commit.
