 /**
- * Remembers a layout and appends when only the tail grew. A lane-width change, a height change,
- * or a shorter list replaces the whole layout and reports [structuralChange].
+ * Remembers a layout.
+ *
+ * Same [contentEpoch], lane geometry, and [count] returns the previous layout and does not call
+ * [heightOf] or [spanOf]. A longer list with that same epoch appends. Anything else rebuilds and
+ * reports [structuralChange] so the viewport can stay on its anchor in the same measure.
+ *
+ * Harmony: the epoch replaces the per-item prefix check. Scroll frames keep the epoch, so a large
+ * shelf does not allocate a height for every row. Callers bump it when a committed cover crosses
+ * the wide/tall band or the items lambda changes. Lane widths are compared on their own and always
+ * rebuild, including when a wide cover starts or stops spanning two lanes.
  */
